---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../lib/site/config";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — pre-launch notice"
  description="How The Wedding Nest's preview handles planning choices, and the privacy decisions being prepared before real enquiries open."
>
  <article>
    <header class="page-hero on-dark">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-8 py-24 md:py-32">
        <p class="eyebrow text-saffron">Before enquiries open</p>
        <h1 class="mt-6 text-[length:var(--text-headline)] text-ivory">Privacy, in plain words.</h1>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg text-stone">
          This is a pre-launch notice for review. This preview does not accept real enquiries. Live
          storage, notifications and retention operations must be verified before intake opens.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-8 py-16 md:py-24 text-ink">
      <section aria-labelledby="preview-privacy" class="max-w-2xl">
        <h2 id="preview-privacy" class="text-3xl">
          What stays in this browser
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
          The planner can remember non-personal planning choices for seven days. Names, phone
          numbers, venue details, notes and consent are not saved in that draft. Start again clears
          it. Copy planning choices excludes those private fields too. Please do not enter sensitive
          information or real contact details in this preview.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="future-enquiries" class="mt-12 max-w-2xl">
        <h2 id="future-enquiries" class="text-3xl">
          When real enquiries open
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
          The planned enquiry collects your name, phone number, preferred way to talk and the event
          choices you provide so the team can respond. Date, budget, venue and notes may remain
          undecided. Optional marketing consent is separate; no marketing delivery is active.
          Production storage, notification providers, access and the final notice still require
          review. Test submissions belong only in the separately labelled fictional-data
          environment.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="retention" class="mt-12 max-w-2xl">
        <h2 id="retention" class="text-3xl">
          The retention decision
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
          The owner has selected 90 days from the date an enquiry is explicitly marked unsuccessful.
          This does not classify old or active enquiries as unsuccessful. Booked-client records need
          a separate rule. No live cleanup is active; the operator process and treatment of pending
          notifications must be settled before this becomes an operational retention notice.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-contact" class="mt-12 max-w-2xl">
        <h2 id="privacy-contact" class="text-3xl">
          Privacy requests
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
          For access, correction or deletion requests, contact{" "}
          <a class="link-underline break-words" href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>
            {SITE.email}
          </a>
          . Share only enough information to identify your enquiry. Please do not send passwords,
          identity documents or unrelated sensitive information.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
